1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
JavaScript is dying — and TypeScript is the murderer. And some people are celebrating this!

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:16,000
TypeScript crossed 78% developer adoption in 2024 — top 3 most-loved on Stack Overflow. Big achievement, but what's the problem?

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Juniors are learning TypeScript directly — without understanding JavaScript's foundation. You're building without a base.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:36,000
TypeScript is just a superset of JavaScript. Remove the types — you get vanilla JS underneath. Weak JS means hollow TS.

5
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Companies think TypeScript = better code. But type safety is just a tool — it can't replace thinking. Turning off strict mode and using 'any' everywhere is just cheating!

6
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Learn JavaScript first — only then will TypeScript's real power unlock. Strong foundation, strong building.

7
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Comment below — did you learn JavaScript first or jumped straight to TypeScript? Follow CodeOrCap. Stop Guessing. Start Knowing.
